1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:29,340
It all comes down to timing.

3
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:33,180
Opportunity knocks but once.

4
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:36,540
What? They're both gone?

5
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:38,940
It's like they already know exactly
what that Masked Guy did.

6
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:40,380
They seem totally in the loop.

7
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:41,820
I wanted to ask, do you know

8
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:44,700
about this Mysterious Masked Guy?

9
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:47,100
Do you know what connection he has to your Chengnan Team?

10
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:49,020
So you're the one with the mask, huh?

11
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:50,460
And you must be Mark.

12
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:51,900
Glad you know.

13
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:54,300
Give me back Chuck's Nuclear Fission! Now!

14
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:56,220
I say we just draw straws to decide.

15
00:01:56,400 --> 00:01:57,660
That's actually a good idea.

16
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Episode 15

17
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,820
You guys are acting like total scumbags.

18
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:10,140
All you do is call us cheaters and thugs.

19
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:11,580
Do you have any proof

20
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:13,500
that the Masked Guy has anything to do with us?

21
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:16,380
I've already cut you way too much slack.

22
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,780
If you take one more step forward,

23
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,220
I won't be so nice.

24
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:24,060
You losing to some Masked Guy is none of our business!

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:25,980
Why are you coming here and causing trouble?

26
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:28,380
You're just lashing out because you're desperate!

27
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,600
You guys lost, so you sent a Masked Guy to mess with us!

28
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:31,740
That's even more desperate!

29
00:02:32,010 --> 00:02:32,450
What're you doing?

30
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:33,630
What're you doing?

31
00:02:33,640 --> 00:02:34,620
What do you think you're doing?

32
00:02:35,080 --> 00:02:36,540
You... you...

33
00:02:37,660 --> 00:02:38,460
You want a piece of me?

34
00:02:40,060 --> 00:02:41,820
You barge into someone else's Camp to start a fight,

35
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:43,740
and you think you're in the right?

36
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:45,660
Especially when you've got no reason at all!

37
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:48,540
I already told you, we do have a reason.

38
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:52,790
What reason? You call that a reason? Some "Masked Guy"?

39
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:56,700
You've got no witnesses and no evidence.

40
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:00,450
Hmph. Been watching too much Sherlock Holmes or what?

41
00:03:04,640 --> 00:03:05,340
Come in.

42
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:07,260
Manager Ma.

43
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:09,180
Oh! Mark.

44
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:13,510
This Player of yours made a serious mistake.
Take him back with you.

45
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,380
If it weren't out of respect for your Coach Tony,

46
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:19,660
your whole Team would've been out of here long ago.

47
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:22,140
But! I still have to warn you.

48
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:25,020
If there's a next time,

49
00:03:25,480 --> 00:03:26,790
you'll be kicked out for good.

50
00:03:28,340 --> 00:03:30,300
I won't care about any old connections.

51
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:32,590
Is that perfectly clear?

52
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:34,990
Loud and clear.

53
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:37,500
Go on.

54
00:03:51,970 --> 00:03:52,860
Sorry, Captain.

55
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:56,220
You did it all for Jianghai Team, right?

56
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,810
But don't go pulling dumb stunts like that again.

57
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:46,620
So nobody drew the short straw?

58
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:59,580
Teddy, you're the best Player left. It's up to you.

59
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,420
I feel a lot better knowing it's you.

60
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:06,780
Captain, I've got a suggestion.

61
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:10,940
Doing it this way clearly isn't working.

62
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,940
We should just tell the Coach and have
him hurry back here to deal with this.

63
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:17,340
We still don't know

64
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:19,260
where this Masked Guy even came from.

65
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:21,180
Once the Coach is back,

66
00:05:22,120 --> 00:05:24,060
the Masked Guy might just disappear for good.

67
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:26,580
And then our Yo-Yos are as good as gone!

68
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:29,340
Besides,

69
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:32,700
we should handle our own problems.

70
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:35,580
Otherwise, we'll just look like a joke.

71
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:38,940
Well, there's someone hiding in his tent sleeping right now.

72
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,860
Isn't he afraid of being a laughingstock?

73
00:05:41,880 --> 00:05:42,850
Leo's really gone too far.

74
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:45,580
I'm disappointed in him too.

75
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:11,580
Meatball!

76
00:06:16,840 --> 00:06:20,700
What gives? Why'd you wake me up in the middle of the night?

77
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,140
Huge news!

78
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:24,060
So I was just about to go to the bathroom,

79
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:26,280
but when I got to the Dock,

80
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:27,900
I saw this super intense light show on the bridge.

81
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:31,260
And if I had to guess, that had to be Leo.

82
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:34,140
And I thought it was something serious.

83
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:37,500
Leo's up early practicing at this critical moment.

84
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:39,420
Doesn't this just prove

85
00:06:39,880 --> 00:06:41,570
that Leo's actually getting ready to take on the Masked Guy?

86
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:46,620
No way. He wouldn't even take part in the draw.

87
00:06:48,020 --> 00:06:49,570
Maybe he wants to surprise us.

88
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:53,360
Let's go see!

89
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,260
Nah, I'm dead tired.

90
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:56,700
Come on, Meatball! Let's go!

91
00:06:57,340 --> 00:06:58,140
Let's check it out, come on!

92
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:07,740
Hurry up!

93
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:17,820
Mickey.

94
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:21,630
Are you getting your dreams mixed up with reality again?

95
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:23,580
Are you totally confused?

96
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:25,500
But I know I saw him!

97
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:32,700
Oh, man!

98
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:43,260
I told you it was just a dream,
but you wouldn't believe me.

99
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,620
Look, Leo's right there sleeping.

100
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,900
But I swear I just saw that he wasn't in his tent!

101
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:53,460
You're clearly imagining things about Leo.

102
00:07:54,760 --> 00:07:58,070
And now you're seeing things. Man, that's just sad.

103
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:02,460
Ah, Just go back to sleep.

104
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:23,580
1, 2, 3, 4!

105
00:08:25,480 --> 00:08:25,980
Halt!

106
00:08:27,800 --> 00:08:28,860
Face Straight!

107
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,740
Dress right!

108
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:34,620
Eyes front!

109
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:36,060
At ease!

110
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:37,500
Attention!

111
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:39,150
Jianghai Team!

112
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:40,380
Victory!

113
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:41,340
Dismissed!

114
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:48,540
I'm beat.

115
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:53,340
Teddy! Why haven't you gone for the Duel yet?

116
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:54,270
If you're late,

117
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,740
the Masked Guy might just disappear!

118
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:59,580
Captain, my stomach's been killing me since I woke up.

119
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:01,980
I've been in the bathroom this whole time.

120
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:05,340
I think... there's no way I can go to the duel now.

121
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:07,740
But I totally saw you this morning and you were fine!

122
00:09:09,160 --> 00:09:12,060
You have no idea the pain I was in on that toilet!

123
00:09:13,180 --> 00:09:14,940
You're just scared, so you're faking it!

124
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:17,820
Me? Scared? Scared of what?

125
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:21,660
If I were scared, I wouldn't have
taken part in the draw last night!

126
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,020
Some people didn't even take part in the draw last night.

127
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:26,430
Why don't you go nag him?

128
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:28,860
Alright. We're running out of time.

129
00:09:29,300 --> 00:09:30,780
Teddy, can you handle this or not?

130
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:36,060
Look, you're not holding your stomach anymore.
You must be fine.

131
00:09:36,520 --> 00:09:38,940
What do you know? Stomach cramps come in waves.

132
00:09:40,360 --> 00:09:41,820
If I go out there in this condition,

133
00:09:42,280 --> 00:09:44,510
I'm basically just handing my
Vortex over to that Masked Guy!

134
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:47,100
Captain!

135
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:49,500
I think it's better if I just go last.

136
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:59,100
Well, then I guess we'll just have to draw straws again.

137
00:10:00,330 --> 00:10:00,930
Hold on.

138
00:10:15,400 --> 00:10:18,300
Leo, on behalf of everyone, I'm begging you.

139
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,140
Please, step up and take down that Masked Guy for us.

140
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,380
I'm afraid that's a lot to ask of me.

141
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
But...

142
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:35,580
Leo.

143
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:38,460
I never thought you'd be such a Coward.

144
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,900
I really misjudged you.

145
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:49,020
If he won't go, I will!

146
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:50,940
Mickey!

147
00:11:06,760 --> 00:11:09,180
Mickey? What happened?

148
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:14,940
What do we do if this keeps happening?

149
00:11:15,880 --> 00:11:18,300
Don't go causing a panic and shaking our morale!

150
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:24,540
Its OK. I know you gave it everything you had.

151
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,460
What could I do?

152
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,860
Who knew he'd use that Thousand Dragons Rising move again?

153
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:21,180
Captain, I...

154
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:16,380
It's Sis!

155
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:22,620
Mini.

156
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:26,460
I know even if you went, it wouldn't matter.

157
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:29,340
But I don't have any better ideas.

158
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,700
Then we swap people out.

159
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:37,500
Teddy, honestly, you're the only one who has a shot.

160
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:39,870
Otherwise, everyone's gonna lose their Yo-Yos,

161
00:12:39,880 --> 00:12:42,270
and you'll end up having to go anyway.

162
00:12:42,280 --> 00:12:43,740
We all agreed on this rule together.

163
00:12:43,990 --> 00:12:45,180
How can you just back out now?

164
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:49,300
Mickey, Don't cause a scene.

165
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:54,300
Captain, tomorrow I'll give it absolutely everything I've got.

166
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,140
Who knows, maybe I'll even perform better than I think.

167
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:01,500
Mini.

168
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:04,380
Thank you.

169
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:19,260
Captain!

170
00:13:21,160 --> 00:13:22,140
Don't wake everyone up.

171
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:27,420
Captain, I couldn't sleep either.

172
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:42,300
You're all up so early?

173
00:14:43,720 --> 00:14:45,660
Everyone's here to see you off.

174
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:48,060
The Captain and I were up all night.

175
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:49,020
Me too!

176
00:14:49,960 --> 00:14:50,460
None of us could sleep.

177
00:14:51,680 --> 00:14:53,820
Unlike Leo, who's in there snoring away without a care.

178
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:56,220
He was gone first thing this morning.

179
00:14:56,680 --> 00:14:57,660
He's totally heartless.

180
00:14:58,600 --> 00:14:59,580
No sense of loyalty.

181
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:00,790
He chickened out.

182
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:01,980
Scared of his own shadow.

183
00:15:02,140 --> 00:15:02,940
He's got no humanity.

184
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:04,380
Who's got no humanity?

185
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:05,820
Coach Tony!

186
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:07,930
We were just talking about Leo.

187
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:09,660
Leo?

188
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,060
What's up with Leo?

189
00:15:12,520 --> 00:15:13,500
Well, Coach, it's like this.

190
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:22,140
Enough.

191
00:15:25,480 --> 00:15:27,420
Everyone, just calm down.

192
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:30,300
I should get going, too.

193
00:15:31,690 --> 00:15:32,700
Hold on.

194
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:36,030
I'll go with you.

195
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:38,940
Coach, if that Masked Guy sees you,

196
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:40,380
he might just disappear for good.

197
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:42,300
And then all of our Yo-Yos

198
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:44,220
will be gone forever!

199
00:15:45,440 --> 00:15:46,540
Then I can't just let Mini

200
00:15:46,600 --> 00:15:48,260
go and hand him another Yo-Yo for nothing.

201
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:50,940
Shawn.

202
00:15:52,360 --> 00:15:54,300
Chuck! Your Nuclear Fission!

203
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:58,140
Mickey! Ferris Wheel!

204
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,060
And also, also, also...

205
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,460
Oh! Matthew's Shockwave!

206
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,340
Captain! Here's your Speed Dragon!

207
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:09,180
Shawn, how'd you get all these back?

208
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:12,060
You think dressing like that

209
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:13,500
is what it takes to beat the Masked Guy?

210
00:16:14,240 --> 00:16:16,350
Shawn, wait, you mean these Yo-Yos...

211
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,780
Did you steal them back from the Masked Guy?

212
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,190
Shawn.

213
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:22,140
You actually look pretty good dressed up as a girl.

214
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:25,020
Shawn, I seriously can't thank you enough!

215
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:26,350
Alright, alright! Everyone quiet down.

216
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:27,670
Let Shawn explain.

217
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:29,820
No need to thank me.

218
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:31,230
Leo was the one who won these back for you all.

219
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:40,860
Sorry.

220
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:43,740
Coach, I didn't tell everyone

221
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,140
because we had to keep it a Secret.

222
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:49,980
The moment the Masked Guy showed up,

223
00:16:50,440 --> 00:16:52,380
I could tell he was bad news.

224
00:16:53,320 --> 00:16:55,740
Mark and Leo are the 2 best Players on the Team.

225
00:16:56,680 --> 00:16:57,660
And since Mark lost,

226
00:16:58,120 --> 00:16:59,580
Leo couldn't afford to lose, too.

227
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:01,980
Otherwise, no one would be able to beat him.

228
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:04,380
So I racked my brain

229
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:06,020
and came up with a brilliant strategy.

230
00:17:06,030 --> 00:17:07,180
And that was...

231
00:17:07,240 --> 00:17:09,180
to keep the enemy in the dark.

232
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:13,500
Lure him in deep, retreat when he advances,
strike where he's unprepared.

233
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:16,680
Know yourself and know your enemy,
and you'll win every battle!

234
00:17:17,690 --> 00:17:18,200
Everyone get it?

235
00:17:21,160 --> 00:17:23,810
Wow! You've got some brains!

236
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:26,940
That's way too vague.

237
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:29,340
That's way too deep. I didn't get any of that.

238
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:31,740
Alright, let Leo explain it himself.

239
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:37,020
After Mark lost, I figured
I should be the one to step up.

240
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:38,950
But Shawn strongly advised against it.

241
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:40,380
He said we should keep the Opponent guessing first.

242
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:42,780
He even dressed up like a
village girl to spy on him in secret.

243
00:17:43,720 --> 00:17:45,180
He used a little DV cam he had on him

244
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:46,590
to record Mickey and Matthew's

245
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:47,690
Duels against the Masked Guy.

246
00:17:47,700 --> 00:17:49,980
I watched the footage over and over,

247
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:53,340
and finally I figured out the
pattern in the Masked Guy's Moves.

248
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,220
I realized that when he plays with two Yo-Yos,

249
00:17:57,160 --> 00:17:58,620
he always uses one of them

250
00:17:59,080 --> 00:17:59,740
to distract his opponent.

251
00:17:59,750 --> 00:18:00,990
And then with the other one,

252
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,940
he uses a string manipulation trick to seize the opening.

253
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:06,780
It creates a powerful vortex that
separates the Yo-Yo from its string.

254
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:08,700
That's how he snatches his opponent's Yo-Yo

255
00:18:09,160 --> 00:18:10,620
and gets it into his own hand so easily.

256
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:13,020
So I decided to use a feint as well.

257
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:15,820
Every time, I'd fake one move

258
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:18,820
and then suddenly switch it up,
so his snatch attempt would fail.

259
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:13,020
Finally, he was forced to use both
hands to try and trap my Yo-Yo.

260
00:19:13,480 --> 00:19:16,380
That's when I made my real move
and changed my technique.

261
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:27,420
Thousand Dragons Rising!

262
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:29,360
Lightning Shift!

263
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:05,820
And just like that,
his Thousand Dragons Rising attack failed.

264
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:10,140
The two Yo-Yos got tangled up
and wrapped around each other.

265
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:12,060
The Masked Guy totally surrendered.

266
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:15,110
He handed over all the Yo-Yos.

267
00:20:15,880 --> 00:20:19,740
But before he left, the Masked Guy said, "We'll meet again."

268
00:20:20,200 --> 00:20:22,620
Wow! Leo, you're absolutely amazing!

269
00:20:24,040 --> 00:20:25,500
Leo, I'm your biggest fan!

270
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:26,940
Go on, get outta here!

271
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:28,860
Leo, thank you.

272
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:31,260
Leo, you're so cool.

273
00:20:33,820 --> 00:20:35,100
That's so cheesy!

274
00:20:38,520 --> 00:20:40,380
Leo, seriously, congrats.

275
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:50,520
Actually, the person we really ought to thank is Shawn.

276
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:53,350
Oh yeah, that's right!

277
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:56,270
Shawn! This time, your contribution was absolutely huge.

278
00:20:57,440 --> 00:20:58,140
A Master Strategist!

279
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,060
A Legendary Feat!

280
00:21:00,520 --> 00:21:01,470
Your name will go down in history!

281
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:03,790
Then I guess the only thing left to say is you're Immortal!

282
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:05,120
No, no, no! Please, don't!

283
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:06,780
I'd like to live a few more years, thanks!

284
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:10,590
Alright. Shawn played a crucial role in all of this.

285
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:11,780
A truly vital role.

286
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:12,940
Everyone saw it.

287
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:16,380
Hold on, Coach. Could I have a word with you in private?

